# Hosts that block or rate-limit automated link checkers.
https?://([a-z0-9-]+\.)?linkedin\.com.*
https?://([a-z0-9-]+\.)?xing\.com.*
# 2026-07-27: returns nothing within 60s from GitHub runners, a local checker,
# and a third network path, so the check can neither confirm nor refute these
# URLs. It failed the link check on roughly every second run. The citations in
# skills/web-legal-compliance/references/canada.md are unverified by tooling and
# need a human to confirm them.
https?://laws-lois\.justice\.gc\.ca/.*
https?://help\.malt\.com/.*
https?://www\.malt\.com/.*
https?://support\.upwork\.com/.*
https?://support\.usebraintrust\.com/.*
https?://www\.solcom\.de/.*

# A new main-branch route cannot resolve before its first merge, so a pull
# request that adds a skill or ADR needs a temporary entry here. Repository
# inventory and local links are checked by scripts/validate-readmes.py.
#
# Remove the entry once the branch is merged. An exception left behind stops the
# link check from ever verifying that route again, which is how a genuinely
# broken link would slip through unnoticed.

# These live primary sources reject, reset, or time out on GitHub Actions'
# link-check traffic.
https://www\.mckinsey\.com/careers/interviewing
https://tbrown\.org/11/
https://doi\.org/10\.1177/154193120504900514
https://www\.congress\.gov/
https://www\.isof\.se/download/18\.17dda5f1791cdbd2873a99/1620030264840/Mynd-skrivreg2014-1\.pdf
https://www\.isof\.se/utforska/publikationer/publikationer/2024-01-22-snabba-skrivregler
https://www\.gesetze-im-internet\.de/ddg/
https://www\.gesetze-im-internet\.de/tdddg/
https://www\.cai\.gouv\.qc\.ca/
https://europass\.europa\.eu/en/create-europass-cv
https://portal\.education\.lu/zls

# 2026-07-29: the ISO and ANSI standards stores return 403 to GitHub Actions
# after retries. Keep the official citations for human readers; the automated
# checker cannot verify these sources from its runner network.
https://www\.iso\.org/standard/.*
https://webstore\.ansi\.org/industry/safety-standards/safety-signs-labels

# 2026-07-29: these exact editorial and Canadian government sources exhausted
# the link check's timeout and retry budget. Keep the exclusions narrow so other
# pages on the same hosts remain verifiable.
https://pimpmytype\.com/line-length-line-height/
https://www\.noslangues-ourlanguages\.gc\.ca/writing-tips-plus/spacing
https://our-languages\.canada\.ca/en/writing-tips-plus/spacing
https://ised-isde\.canada\.ca/site/canada-anti-spam-legislation/en
https://ised-isde\.canada\.ca/site/office-consumer-affairs/en/federal-provincial-and-territorial-consumer-affairs-offices
https://www\.priv\.gc\.ca/en/privacy-topics/privacy-laws-in-canada/02_05_d_15/

# 2026-07-23: slow language-institution sources that intermittently time out from
# GitHub runners even with retries; both verified reachable manually.
https://gfds\.de/leerzeichen-und-festabstaende/
https://frageladan\.isof\.se/faqs/23562

# 2026-07-27: the Norwegian language council refuses GitHub runner traffic with a
# connection failure. It broke every open pull request while main stayed green by
# chance; verified reachable manually.
https://sprakradet\.no/.*

# 2026-07-27: GitHub renders pull-request review-comment anchors client-side, so
# --include-fragments can never resolve them from the served HTML. The pull
# request itself is still checked; only the comment anchor is skipped.
https://github\.com/.*/pull/[0-9]+\#discussion_r[0-9]+
